# Marktplaats listings

Use the seller’s logged-in Playwright/Chrome session. Never ask for or type the password. Do not post a card that is `concept` or not in stock.

When a card should go live: place the ad, then set `marktplaatsUrl` and drop `concept`. Until then it stays `concept: true` with no listing URL (shop shows **Not yet available to buy**).

## Always

- **Photos:** slab front first, slab back second (`*_front.jpg` then `*_back.jpg`).
- **Category:** Hobby en Vrije tijd → Verzamelkaartspellen | Pokémon.
- **Kenmerken:** Zo goed als nieuw, Type Losse kaart, Foil on.
- **Levering:** Ophalen of Verzenden. Pakketgrootte **Brievenbuspakje** (never Klein pakket).
- **Prijs:** Vraagprijs from the site. **Direct Kopen toegestaan** on. Do not turn on Bieden unless asked.
- **Adverteren:** **Gratis** only. Never Plus/Premium unless asked.
- Do not change prices on other live ads.

## Title (copy live ads)

`{Name} {number} {variant} - {Grader} {grade} - {Set}`

Examples: `Zorua 140/086 AR - BGS 9.5 - White Flare Japanese`, `Arceus V Full Art 165/172 - PSA 9 - Brilliant Stars`.

## Description (Lexical editor)

Copy the frozen reference ads below (verbatim snapshots). Do not depend on Marktplaats URLs — those ads disappear when a card sells.

Do **not** `fill()` the description — Marktplaats collapses `\n` into one paragraph. Click the editor, then:

- **Enter** between major sections (creates a new paragraph = visible blank line)
- **Shift+Enter** inside a section (line break, no extra gap — Details bullets, 📦 then 💬, ⭐ then the combine line)
- Bold: the `Mooie …` phrase, **Details:**, **Bekijk ook onze andere advertenties!**. Bold grade / subgrades / pop only when they are a selling point (see Zorua).

**Blank line between every major section.** Details bullets stay tight.

### Pop

Only mention pop when it is **low** (a scarcity argument — tens, like Zorua’s 20). Then: intro `Lage **pop** van **{n}**.` and a Details line `• Pop: {n}`.

Skip pop entirely when it is high / irrelevant (hundreds or thousands — Charizard has none). If unsure, omit.

